hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16000","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, he said, Sa'id ibn Yazid, who is Abu Shuja', informed us, he said, I heard al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Hadrami narrating from Ali ibn Rabah, from Nashira ibn Sumayy al-Yazani, he said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, say on the day of al-Jabiya while addressing people: Allah the Mighty and Majestic made me treasurer of this wealth and its divider. Then he said: Rather, Allah divides it, and I begin with the family of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then their noblest. So he assigned to the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten thousand, except Juwayriya and Safiya and Maymuna. So A'isha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be just among us. So Umar was just among them. Then he said: I begin with my companions, the first Muhajirun, for we were expelled from our homes unjustly and aggressively, then their noblest. So he assigned to the people of Badr among them five thousand, and to whoever witnessed Badr of the Ansar four thousand, and to whoever witnessed Uhud three thousand. He said: Whoever hastened in hijra, giving is hastened to him, and whoever was slow in hijra, giving is slowed to him. So let no man blame but the resting place of his camel. And I apologize to you concerning Khalid ibn al-Walid: I commanded him to withhold this wealth for the weak of the Muhajirun, but he gave the strong and the noble and the eloquent, so I removed him and appointed Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah. So Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughira said: By Allah, you have not excused yourself, O Umar ibn al-Khattab. You removed a worker employed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sheathed a sword unsheathed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), placed a banner raised by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), severed kinship, and envied the cousin. So Umar ibn al-Khattab said: You are near of kin, young in age, angered on behalf of your cousin."
